arantees: reject unknown properties, require nonblank identifiers/descriptions/targets, constrain allowed_targets entries, and define policy_checks item structure. Evidence: all three files under schemas/ currently omit additionalProperties=false; tool-metadata.schema.json:7-13 and invocation-envelope.schema.json:7-13 accept empty strings; decision-receipt.schema.json:13 leaves policy_checks items unconstrained. Human-visible behavior: clients can pass schema validation but still receive a policy denial, or accept malformed receipt objects as schema-valid. Smallest authoritative surface: the three schema JSON files and schema/CLI contract tests. P2—Expand decision-matrix coverage for target mismatch and wildcard boundaries, non-idempotent mutation, reviewable missing-trace input, critical missing-trace input, tool-id mismatch, and blank metadata/envelope fields. Evidence: tests/policy_decisions.rs:34-64 covers only three paths, while src/policy.rs:29-157 contains multiple distinct deny/review branches and src/types.rs:56-90 contains validation branches. Human-visible behavior: regressions in denial and review boundaries may ship undetected. Smallest authoritative surface: tests/policy_decisions.rs and tests/cli_contract.rs only.",
